  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Design Details**\n\nI\'ve finally gotten my hands on the complete design specification! I\'m now meticulously dissecting every detail in `/public/assets/aistudio/Image_16_f1c299ca.markdown` to align it perfectly with the user\'s request. It\'s a comprehensive document, and I\'m cross-referencing everything to ensure complete harmony.\n\n\n**Defining Brand Parameters**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the brand parameters. \"Elessa Architectural Systems\" is the central brand name, translating to \"\330\247\331\204\330\263\330\247\" in Farsi. This brand focuses on elite architectural solutions, including automated entryways, glass railings, smart facades, and electric shutters. My target audience is architects and developers. I aim to convey reliability and technological advancement.\n\n\n**Incorporating RTL Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating right-to-left (RTL) elements for the Persian market. My focus is on ensuring a seamless user experience. I\'ve been reviewing the design spec in detail and am specifically studying how visual elements, from navigation to phone callouts, should flow from right to left. Also, I\'m considering a clean language switcher for versatility.\n\n\n**Prioritizing RTL Focus**\n\nI\'m now fully committed to a pure Persian RTL design, as specified. After scrutinizing the spec, I\'m ditching any top-bar language switcher and considering a subtle `EN / \331\201\330\247` toggle in the footer if *absolutely* necessary, prioritizing the spec\'s directive for authentic Persian RTL. The brand\'s tech specifications, using Latin units like `EL-S400` or `16 mm`, will be presented within the RTL flow, as the spec indicates, keeping the app experience cohesive.\n\n\n**Implementing RTL Layouts**\n\nI\'m now diving into the precise RTL layout, specifically with the Persian brand in mind. I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy: bold hero titles with emerald gradient spans, flowing right to left. I\'m also implementing RTL for chips, filter tags, and input labels with the appropriate margin. The design strictly follows the spec by using the exact Latin technical codes within an executive Persian RTL experience.\n\n**Incorporating Exact Color Tokens**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in using the *exact* color tokens from the specification, ensuring brand consistency. I\'m meticulously implementing the canvas background colors, `#FAFCFB`, `#f8f9ff`, and white. Also, I\'m integrating the muted surface color and the primary/deep emerald tones, adhering to all the specified color codes.\n\n\n**Specifying Color Palettes**\n\nI\'m now deep in the specification\'s color palette, carefully extracting and applying the color codes. I\'m focusing on the interplay of Emerald, Slate, and Mint tones. I\'m checking contrast ratios, especially for the CTA button\'s linear gradient, ensuring WCAG AA compliance. I\'m also incorporating glassmorphic navigation styles with subtle blur effects.\n\n\n\n**Refining Elevation & Shapes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the refined elevation and shape details. I\'ve focused on ensuring the visual hierarchy is clear. Level 1 cards are white with a subtle border and shadow. Interactive catalog tiles have a distinct hover effect. For glassmorphic navigation and the sticky quotation bar, I\'ve used appropriate transparency and blur, including crisp white edges. I\'m also ensuring the specified pill buttons, product display cards, and input fields each feature their requested rounded corners and borders.\n\n\n**Loading Font Families**\n\nI\'m now integrating the specified font families into the project. I\'m loading **Vazirmatn**, **Plus Jakarta Sans**, and **JetBrains Mono** from Google Fonts. I\'m carefully setting the line heights to optimize Persian script readability, with `leading-[1.45]` for display headings and `leading-[1.8]` for body copy. The main hero titles are styled with high-weight font and the emerald gradient span, emphasizing key terms as requested.\n\n\n**Designing Architectural Screens**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing four cohesive architectural screens. I\'m starting with the Home screen (\"\330\265\331\201\330\255\331\207 \330\247\330\265\331\204\333\214\"), featuring a daylight architectural hero image with an emerald gradient accent. I\'ll implement a 16:9 focal photo, a clear value proposition, and prominent CTAs for consultation and catalog viewing, to drive engagement.\n\n\n**Constructing Screen Elements**\n\nI\'m now building out the main elements for the architectural screens. I\'m focusing on the first Home screen, starting with a daylight architectural hero image enhanced by an emerald gradient accent. I\'ll implement a 16:9 focal photo, a clear value proposition, and prominent CTAs for consultation and catalog viewing to drive user engagement. Also, I\'ll showcase asymmetric architectural systems in a bento showcase of the 4 core divisions.\n\n\n**Developing Filterable Catalogs**\n\nI\'m now implementing the interactive search and filter functionality, specifically by application type. I\'m building ultra-clean 16:10 visual cards with frosted-glass category labels, brief spec breakdowns, and estimated pricing, all with rounded corners. Clicking will lead to a detailed product technical specification screen featuring high-resolution photography and a technical spec list that matches the specific specification.\n\n\n**Constructing Product Specs**\n\nI\'m now building the product technical specification screens and adding them to the quotation estimator. I\'m focusing on \"Projects\" which is a filterable showcase of completed commercial towers, and the interactive Price Estimator and Quotation Request. I am implementing one-click project quotes, with an update of the glassmorphic floating sticky bar. The system will feature all the specs requested and is a crucial addition!\n\n\n**Designing Quotation System**\n\nI\'m now building out the core interactive quotation system, adhering strictly to the specs. I\'m focusing on the input forms with white fields, right-aligned labels, and precise RTL layout for the Persian market. I\'m implementing real-time calculation and an interactive confirmation, all from client-side deterministic engineering formulas, ensuring accuracy. I\'m incorporating the specific element requests, from technical details to visual elements.\n\n\n**Refining UI Header**\n\nI\'m now implementing the top bar header per specification. It will be a glassmorphic floating element with three zones in RTL layout: a brand wordmark on the right, four navigation links in the center, and a primary CTA on the left. I\'m focusing on simplicity and functional design, avoiding any unnecessary elements.\n\n\n**Generating Visual Assets**\n\nI\'m now generating all visual assets for this phase in one batch. I\'ve inventoried the needs for the Hero, Product Catalog, and Projects sections. I\'m focusing on six specific daylight-infused architectural photos, and also focusing on ultra-clean, frosted-glass labels for product cards, and clean typographic separators for metadata.\n\n\n**Creating Visual Assets**\n\nI\'m now in the final stage of creating assets. I am generating ultra-high-quality architectural photographs to match the precise aesthetic. I\'ve focused on four product shots (glass railings, smart facades, polycarbonate shutters, and architectural lobbies). Each uses the right angle and right lighting, adhering to the given specifications, so they are ready for immediate integration into the system.\n\n\n"
