  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Marveling at Aesthetics**\n\nI am captivated by the six architectural photographs! The play of light is exquisite, highlighting the crystal-clear glass and the interplay of travertine/limestone hues. The crisp anodized aluminum, the telescopic doors, the concealed U-channel glass railing and cantilevered spider glass canopy are exceptionally well-executed.\n\n\n**Detailing Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the specific visual elements and their corresponding file paths. The transparent polycarbonate security shutter and the double-height lobby of the luxury tower particularly stand out as matching the design system perfectly. To make it reusable, I\'ve noted the exact paths to each image from the system, including the hero entrance and glass railing, in the system. I\'m now transitioning to planning the modular codebase for Phase 2 implementation.\n\n\n**Defining System Specifications**\n\nI\'m deep in the implementation details. I\'ve set the description to \"Elessa Architectural Systems\" and preserved important capabilities. Now I\'m configuring the HTML with RTL support and specific font loading from Google Fonts: Vazirmatn, Plus Jakarta Sans, and JetBrains Mono. I\'ve synced meta tags. I am now working on CSS, including Tailwind import and defining precise design tokens as CSS variables based on the Elessa design spec. The exact colors and styles are being established as reusable variables.\n\n\n**Establishing Design Tokens**\n\nI am now meticulously defining elevation classes and their corresponding styles within the CSS. I\'m focusing on creating a reusable system that aligns perfectly with the Elessa design specifications. These classes, such as `.surface-card-1`, `.surface-card-2`, `.glass-surface`, `.btn-primary-glow`, and `.input-elessa`, are being carefully crafted with precise color values, box shadows, and hover effects, ensuring visual consistency across the system. This system will maintain clean and performant code.\n\n\n**Defining Input and Data**\n\nI\'m now incorporating detailed product data into `/src/data/catalog.ts`. This involves specifying domain-specific technical details in both Persian and Latin script for six architectural product systems. I\'m focusing on attributes such as radius, border colors, and `prefers-reduced-motion` for inputs. The technical specifications cover products across four categories: automatic doors, glass railings, smart facades, and electric shutters.\n\n\n**Incorporating Product Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed product data for Elessa\'s offerings. I\'m focusing on incorporating specifications for the SP350 glass canopy with smart spider facade and the EL-PC90 transparent polycarbonate electric shutter. The system uses a feature-description / measurement setup for product detail, also including finish options with hex codes, glass configurations, and base pricing details in Toman for accurate calculations. I am ensuring that the client-side calculator integrates seamlessly with technical parameters! I am now focusing on four architectural projects to build out as case studies. I\'ve also incorporated a zero-broken-image policy for component `/src/components/ResilientImage.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing the Homepage**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/src/components/Header.tsx` component, strictly adhering to the \"Top Bar Contract\". I\'ve established three distinct zones: brand mark, navigation links (Persian text!), and a primary CTA. The mobile hamburger drawer is also being implemented for compact display on smaller screens. I\'m building out the homepage\'s hero section, creating a 12-column RTL layout with a bold Persian headline, emerald gradient text, and a primary CTA.\n\n\n**Implementing Homepage Details**\n\nI am now structuring the homepage with the hero section incorporating a secondary button for product catalog access and a German DIN/EN trust mention in the body. I\'ve designed the hero with a full-bleed 16:9 entrance photo in a rounded frame and a glassmorphic technical spec readout. I am next integrating a full-width white band with engineering metrics, a 4-column strip with numbers using the tabular-nums style.\n\n\n**Refining UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now refining the user interface elements for the catalog and product details. I\'m focusing on high contrast, designing a deep slate banner with an emerald accent CTA. The catalog filter chips are being styled to match the design spec, using slate tints and emerald highlights. I am also implementing application filter selects and an instant search input, adhering to the design specifications.\n\n\n**Developing Product Views**\n\nI\'m now focused on the display cards, making sure they\'re visually appealing and informative, using a rounded frame, frosted-glass labels, and concise metadata. I\'m also working on a technical specification screen/modal. This includes a finish swatch selector and an interactive technical specification table with right-aligned Persian descriptions and left-aligned numeric values. I\'ve also added an estimator and an \"Add to Estimate\" button.\n\n\n**Constructing Interactive Calculator**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the interactive price estimator. This includes a catalog display with item adjustments and a live configurator for custom specifications. The system is designed to calculate glass weight, leaf count, drive torque, channel depth, and an itemized cost in Persian Toman, all within the live engineering card. I\'ve also implemented an RTL quotation form that generates a downloadable, printable pre-invoice with a deterministic reference ID.\n\n\n"
